id: pm-screen-buon
title: Refuse sparse arrays longer than the traversal budget before schema validation
description: "guardSubmitted bounded visited entries but not array length, so a sparse new Array(2 ** 31) passed the guard and schema validation would iterate every empty slot before the schema's max check. Same class CodeRabbit raised on pm-reduce (fixed there in bf3dff0); pm-case and pm-glossary already bound array length."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: dos,input-guard,privacy
created_at: "2026-11-09T12:57:46.112Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-10T13:42:06.579Z"
assignee: "harness:claude-code"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "Sparse arrays (keys not exactly 0..length-1, including new Array(2**31)) are refused with invalid_input before schema validation; Dense arrays are accepted within the aggregate node budget: a 262143-entry array passes and 262144 refuses; Every graph visit consumes the aggregate budget: shared array and shared object graphs past 262144 visits refuse, and each regression fails on revert"
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T12:57:56.384Z","harness:claude-code","Revert proof: the new test 'guardSubmitted refuses sparse arrays whose length exceeds the traversal budget' fails without the bound and passes with it; test/edge.test.ts passes in full."
  "2026-11-09T15:05:09.653Z","harness:claude-code","Correction after CodeRabbit PRRT_kwDOVll0Ws61TTim and a full-suite run: the per-array cap of 32768 from e345c7a broke the existing contract test 'aggregate node scanning bounds shared graphs and primitive arrays', which allows a dense array of 262143 entries (only the edge file had been run). Many sparse arrays below that cap (127 x 32768 holes) also still passed. The guard now charges each array's holes (length minus present entries; present entries are charged when visited) to the existing 262144 aggregate node budget, with no per-array cap. Full suite 82/82; the holes regression fails against main's guard and passes restored."
  "2026-11-09T17:25:51.018Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit PRRT_kwDOVll0Ws61W80k (IMPORTANT): the holes charge counted Object.keys, which named properties inflate. The class is now closed by accepting only arrays whose keys are exactly 0..length-1 (JSON arrays never have holes); the length is checked against the 262144 aggregate node budget before the keys are listed. This also closes values inherited from Array.prototype through a hole (the sibling finding on pm-unit). The documented dense 262143 boundary is unchanged. 'guardSubmitted accepts only dense JSON arrays within the aggregate node budget' fails against the holes-charge version; full suite 82/82."
  "2026-11-10T13:40:47.833Z",claude-orchestrator,"Orchestrator fix febb17a: CI's review-revert gate failed ('Expected test assertion failure in src/privacy.ts'). The node-budget mutation (++nodes <= 262144 -> ++nodes >= 0) was no longer caught, because the up-front array-length charge added in f9208eb also refuses the all-array DAG. Objects never take that charge, so test/round2.test.ts now also submits a 24^4 shared object graph. Mutation: 0 pass / 1 fail with 'Every graph visit must consume a finite budget'. Code: 1/0. Full npm test 82/0; revert-gate 10/10 reverts detected; review-revert-gate 32 defects detected, all restored tests pass."
  "2026-11-10T13:42:06.577Z",claude-orchestrator,"Acceptance criteria corrected (CodeRabbit PRRT_kwDOVll0Ws61a8Qi): the original 32768 per-array cap was replaced on 11-09 by charging the array length to the aggregate node budget, plus a dense-array check. The criteria now describe the guard that shipped. The comments above keep the history."
files[2]{path,scope}:
  src/privacy.ts,project
  test/edge.test.ts,project
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  node --test test/edge.test.ts,project,"harness:claude-code","2026-11-09T12:57:51.480Z",local_mutation,fix/bound-sparse-array-length
